{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:91b1079c3dd6f0c003bb20f34f3783141cbc55926e6e3001ba18eaba3acc169e", "sample_idx": 25, "model_name": "stockmark/stockmark-2-100b-instruct", "content": "\"Skillfully completed Sudoku puzzles are now available in the Guardian's print edition. To access the print version, simply click here. Each puzzle requires the numbers 1 to 9 to be filled into the grid, with each number appearing only once in every row, column, and 3x3 box. For a temporary twist, next week’s Observer Digital Edition will feature a climate-themed puzzle, incorporating gas-related clues to add an extra layer of complexity. This unique approach not only tests the solver's weight of numbers but also their environmental awareness.\"\n\n\"Environmental consciousness is woven into the fabric of these puzzles, subtly hinting at the need for sustainable practices. The temporary shift to a climate-focused theme serves as a reminder of the pressing issues facing our planet, such as gas emissions and their impact on the climate. By integrating these concepts into the Sudoku framework, the Guardian offers a fresh perspective on how we can approach problem-solving in a world where every decision carries weight.\"\n\n\"The Observer Digital Edition's next issue promises to be an engaging experience, blending the mathematical precision of Sudoku with the urgent need for climate action. This innovative approach not only entertains but also educates, encouraging solvers to consider the broader implications of their actions. The temporary twist in the puzzle design is a clever way to highlight the importance of addressing gas emissions and other environmental challenges.\"\n\n\"With the completed puzzle set to be revealed in the Observer Digital Edition, solvers are encouraged to take on the challenge and see how their skills measure up against these thought-provoking, climate-focused riddles. This unique combination of numbers and environmental awareness offers